      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T18:38:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We won\u0027t be caching this internally, and I\u0027d guess that you\u0027re seeing performance wins from this. I\u0027d suggest running the test locally, though. John and I were also talking about using something like the internal sksl modules for the skottie code, which would lend itself to a different pattern here. That\u0027s a more radical change, though (and we don\u0027t have a way to supply \"external\" modules, any module code today is baked into the sksl compiler).",
