      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T19:10:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alternatively, we can keep the cache but refactor to get rid of templates.  How about something along these lines:\n\n    static SkRuntimeEffect* gEffectCache[kMaxLoops]\n                                        [std::size(gFilters)]\n                                        [std::size(gFractals)];\n\n    auto\u0026 effect \u003d gEffectCache[loops]\n                               [static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(filter)]\n                               [static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(fractal)];\n\n    if (!effect) {\n        effect \u003d make_noise_effect(loops,\n                                   gFilters[static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(filter)],\n                                   gFractals[static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(fractal)])\n                 .release();\n    }\n\n    SkASSERT(effect);\n    return sk_ref_sp(effect);\n    \nI guess we lose thread safety, but this is only being called during revalidation (Animation::seek), which is not thread safe to begin with.\n\n(also we should tweak to only allocate 6 loop indices, since we never use all 20)",
